note={D5. In this context of energy optimization of GSHP systems, both an optimal design of components and an optimal operation of the system as a whole become crucial so that the market gets o the ground in places where it is still lifeless, contributing to attain the targets established by the EU regulations, and to attenuate the global energy problem. Here it is that this PhD work comes into play, dealing with the control and energy optimization of ground source heat pump systems for heating and cooling in an experimental GSHP installation. This PhD work proposes, describes, develops, implements and evaluates a new integrated optimization strategy in order to make the GSHP system operate at its optimal point, which has been tested in situ in the experimental GSHP installation built during GEOCOOL project and upgraded during GROUND-MED project, obtaining signicant energy savings when compared to the standard control operation, up to 35{\%} in the summer season and 53{\%} in the winter season, while keeping the user comfort.},
