note={E3. Key findings.},
note={E4. The key findings of this study include the development of an integrated optimization strategy that achieves significant energy savings, up to 35{\%} in the summer season and 53{\%} in the winter season, while maintaining user comfort. The study also shows that the optimized control strategy outperforms the standard control in terms of energy efficiency..},
note={E5. The study finds that the most restrictive criterion for the maximum system volume is the minimum OFF time, and that a possible solution for tank sizing is to consider a rule of thumb based on the unitary capacity expressed in kW, with a minimum volume provided by the worst-case compressor time. The study also finds that the optimized control strategy is effective in improving energy performance and user comfort in both cooling and heating modes..},
