note={E9. Objectives.},
note={E10. The objectives of this PhD dissertation are to develop an optimal control strategy for the GSHP system, to minimize energy consumption while maintaining user comfort, and to evaluate the performance of the system under different operating conditions. The study also aims to develop an experimental in-situ optimization methodology for the water circulation pumps frequency..},
note={E11. Methods.},
note={E12. The methods used in this study include the development of an integrated optimization strategy, which involves the management of air flow in the fan coil, water mass flow in the internal and external hydraulic systems, and setpoint temperature in the heat pump. The study also employs an experimental in-situ optimization methodology for the water circulation pumps frequency..},
note={E13. The study uses analytical expressions to develop a design guideline for the sizing of buffer tanks, and experiments to evaluate the effectiveness of the optimized control strategy. The study also uses data from a geothermal plant to test the design guideline and the optimized control strategy..},
