note={E16. Results.},
note={E17. The results of this study show that the optimized control strategy achieves significant energy savings, up to 35{\%} in the summer season and 53{\%} in the winter season, while maintaining user comfort. The study also shows that the optimized control strategy outperforms the standard control in terms of energy efficiency..},
note={E18. The study finds that the optimized control strategy is effective in improving energy performance and user comfort in both cooling and heating modes. The study also finds that the design guideline provides a minimum volume for the buffer tank that is sufficient for the heat pump system. The experimental results show that the actual tank temperature tracks the calculated building supply temperature, and that the optimized control strategy saves energy by adjusting the temperature setpoint and the frequency of the water circulation pumps..},
note={E19. The results of the study show that the energy optimization algorithm achieves a 35{\%} improvement in the cooling seasonal performance factor and a 53{\%} improvement in the heating seasonal performance factor, while keeping user comfort..},
