note={E21. Conclusions.},
note={E22. The conclusions of this study are that the developed integrated optimization strategy is effective in minimizing energy consumption while maintaining user comfort, and that the optimized control strategy outperforms the standard control in terms of energy efficiency. The study also concludes that the experimental in-situ optimization methodology for the water circulation pumps frequency is effective in achieving significant energy savings..},
note={E23. The study concludes that the optimized control strategy is effective in improving energy performance and user comfort in both cooling and heating modes. The study also concludes that the design guideline provides a minimum volume for the buffer tank that is sufficient for the heat pump system..},
note={E24. The conclusions of the study are that the energy optimization algorithm developed is effective in achieving energy savings while keeping user comfort, and that the algorithm can be used to optimize the performance of GSHP systems..},
note={E25. The conclusions of the study highlight the effectiveness of the optimized control methodology in improving energy performance while maintaining user comfort, with potential applications to other ground source heat pump installations.}
