note={E13. The local performance section considers local pressure drop and flow boiling heat transfer..},
note={E14. The Chisholm parameter was found to correlate well with the kinetic energy per volume, and the resulting predictions of the pressure drop were accurate to within 10{\%}..},
note={E15. The local flow boiling heat transfer coefficient was compared to flow boiling correlations, and it was found that the saturated nucleate pool boiling correlation by Cooper (1984) and narrow channel flow boiling correlations predicted the experimental data better than traditional flow boiling correlations..},
note={E16. Methodology.},
note={E17. The investigations are both experimental and numerical, with a focus on the experimental part..},
note={E18. The experiments are conducted using classical experimental methods, with measurements taken under steady-state conditions and at least 100 readings for each measured point..},
note={E19. The accuracy of experimental data is ensured by checking for steady state and standard deviation..},
note={E20. The thesis also uses numerical approaches, such as the LMTD method, to evaluate the temperature difference in the boiling section of the evaporator..},
note={E21. Results.},
note={E22. The thesis presents several key findings, including the performance of the evaporator under different operating conditions, the impact of inlet flow geometry on performance, and the estimation of local heat transfer coefficients..},
note={E23. The results show that the brine mass flow rate and heat exchanger size should be selected with care to obtain efficient heat transfer, and that the nucleate boiling model better predicts the performance of the plate heat evaporator..},
note={E24. The thesis also investigates the performance of the evaporator as a two-zone heat exchanger, with separate boiling and superheating sections, and presents a novel technique for estimating local flow boiling heat transfer coefficients.}
}

